Bu sorgu neden full table scan yapıyor? orders tablosunda customer_id üzerinde index var.

EXPLAIN ANALYZE SELECT o.id, c.first_name, c.last_name FROM orders o JOIN customers c ON c.id = o.customer_id WHERE o.created_at > now() - interval '7 days';

Postgres 15, tablo 40M satır.

PR'da şu satıra takıldım:

def get_full_name(self) -> str:
    return f"{self.first_name} {self.last_name}".strip()

middle_name null gelirse double space olmuyor mu? Bir de Django admin'de list_display'e koyunca sort edilemiyor, annotate ile Concat kullanmak daha mı iyi?

Review comment from [[P:Olu]] on my PR says 'this leaks the Hibernate session'. Here's the code:

@Transactional(readOnly = true)
public List<PersonDto> findActive() {
    return personRepository.findByActiveTrue().stream().map(mapper::toDto).toList();
}

Is that true? mapper touches a lazy collection.

# test fixture
users = {
    "alice": {"full_name": "[[P:Aylin Demirci]]", "role": "admin"},
    "bob":   {"full_name": "[[P:Jonas Albrecht]]", "role": "viewer"},
}

pytest says KeyError: 'carol' in test_permissions.py::test_viewer_cannot_delete. Where would 'carol' come from?

Is this naming OK or will reviewers complain?

class PersonNameFormatter {
  static String format(Person p) => '${p.lastName.toUpperCase()}, ${p.firstName}';
}

It's Flutter/Dart. We display names in the Kotlin app the other way round.

Oracle'dan PostgreSQL'e geçiyoruz. Şu sorgu Oracle'da çalışıyor ama Postgres'te hata veriyor:

SELECT * FROM (SELECT e.*, ROWNUM rn FROM employees e WHERE dept_id = 40) WHERE rn BETWEEN 11 AND 20;

LIMIT/OFFSET ile nasıl yazarım, performans farkı olur mu?

Rust borrow checker is yelling at me:

fn display_name(p: &Person) -> &str {
    let s = format!("{} {}", p.first_name, p.last_name);
    &s
}

I get why, but what's the idiomatic fix, return String or Cow<str>?
